-# VXgram
+# VXGram
 
+An Instagram-style social app. **Flutter** (BLoC, clean layers) + **Supabase** (Postgres, Auth, Storage).
+English and Farsi (RTL), light and dark mode.
+
+## Features
+- Sign up / log in / reset password / change password, onboarding, language + theme picker
+- Feed with photo + video posts, **slideshow** for multi-media posts, like, comment, copy link, share, bookmark
+- Create post: up to 10 photos/videos, caption, upload progress, thumbnails, rollback on failure
+- Explore grid + username search
+- Profiles: counts, follow / unfollow, **private accounts** with follow requests, followers / following lists,
+  edit profile, avatar, delete own posts, saved posts
+- Share a post to other users, inbox
+- Notifications: likes, comments, follows, follow requests (confirm / delete in the list), unread badge
+
+## Structure
+```
+vxgram/
+  frontend/vxgram/   Flutter app
+  backend/           Supabase migrations (see backend/README.md)
+```
+Each feature in `lib/features/<name>/` is split into:
+`domain/` (repository interface + entities) -> `data/` (data source interface + Supabase implementation, models,
+repository implementation) -> `bloc/` -> `ui/`. `main.dart` is the only file that knows the concrete classes.
+
+## Run
+1. Create a Supabase project and apply the migrations (`vxgram/backend/README.md`).
+2. Put your Project URL and **anon** key in `vxgram/frontend/vxgram/lib/core/env.dart`
+   (or pass `--dart-define=SUPABASE_URL=... --dart-define=SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=...`).
+3. ```
+   cd vxgram/frontend/vxgram
+   flutter pub get
+   flutter test
+   flutter run
+   ```
+
+## Tests
+BLoC / cubit tests use fake repositories (`test/fakes/`), so they need no network and no Supabase.
